Set up documentation assets for an existing or new repository by mirroring ONLY
the README.md format, Docusaurus website structure, and GitHub Actions -> GitHub
Pages deployment from ${1:https://github.com/<owner>/<reference-repository>}. Do NOT mirror the reference
project's application code, package architecture, tests, Python project setup, or
product-specific implementation. Only the documentation/public-site layer should
be copied structurally; content must be rewritten for the target project.

## Step 0 - Mandatory documentation-site exploration (do this first, miss nothing)
Read these documentation-related files before writing anything, and mirror their
README/Docusaurus/GitHub-Pages structure only:
- README.md (centered header div, badges, section order, documentation tables,
  documentation links, image placement, callouts)
- website/package.json (Docusaurus 3.10.2 classic + faster, React 19, node >=20)
- website/docusaurus.config.js (title/tagline/favicon, url, baseUrl,
  organizationName, projectName, trailingSlash, classic preset, navbar, footer,
  prism languages)
- website/sidebars.js (manual sidebar categories and doc ordering)
- website/src/pages/index.js + index.module.css (docs landing page hero,
  CodeBlock, button, homepage layout)
- website/src/components/HomepageFeatures/index.js + styles.module.css (3 docs
  landing-page feature cards)
- website/src/css/custom.css (Infima color overrides)
- website/docs/*.md (frontmatter, page structure, docs navigation shape)
- website/static/img/, website/static/.nojekyll, website/.gitignore
- .github/workflows/deploy-docs.yaml (GitHub Pages build+deploy jobs)
- assets/ (README/site logo and documentation images only)

Do not use src/, tests/, pyproject.toml, package/runtime code, CLI structure, or
other application files as templates except when describing the target project's
own architecture in README/docs.

